# Task Breakdown: Rendering Engine Polish

## Source Plan
./speckit.rendering-polish.plan

---

## Phase 1: Terminal Capabilities Foundation

### T1.1 — Create internal/termcap/termcap.go
- Define `Capabilities` struct with fields: `SyncOutput bool`, `OSC52 bool`, `ColorProfile colorprofile.Profile`, `DarkBackground bool`
- Define `Detect() (*Capabilities, error)` function that orchestrates all probes
- All probes run sequentially with 100ms timeout each
- Total detection budget: <500ms
- Export package-level `var Current *Capabilities` set once at startup
- **Files:** new `internal/termcap/termcap.go`

### T1.2 — Create internal/termcap/probe.go
- `probeSyncOutput() bool` — send DECRPM query `\x1b[?2026$p`, parse response for mode support
- `probeOSC52() bool` — write a small test payload via OSC 52, verify no error (or check terminal env vars as heuristic: TERM_PROGRAM known to support it)
- `probeColorProfile() colorprofile.Profile` — use `charmbracelet/colorprofile.Detect()` (promote from indirect to direct dep)
- `probeBackgroundColor() (isDark bool)` — send OSC 11 query `\x1b]11;?\x07`, parse RGB response, compute luminance
- All probes work in raw terminal mode using `golang.org/x/term`
- Each probe has its own 100ms timeout via `select` with `time.After`
- **Files:** new `internal/termcap/probe.go`

### T1.3 — Create internal/termcap/clipboard.go
- Define `Clipboard` interface: `WriteAll(string) error`, `ReadAll() (string, error)`
- `OSC52Clipboard` struct: writes `\x1b]52;c;{base64}\x07` to os.Stdout
- `SystemClipboard` struct: wraps `atotto/clipboard` (existing behavior)
- `NewClipboard(caps *Capabilities) Clipboard` factory: returns OSC52 if supported, System otherwise
- OSC 52 payload limit: reject >100KB with fallback to SystemClipboard
- Export `var DefaultClipboard Clipboard` set at startup
- **Files:** new `internal/termcap/clipboard.go`

### T1.4 — Add config fields to Settings
- Add `ColorProfile string` field with yaml tag `color_profile,omitempty`
- Add `Animations *bool` field with yaml tag `animations,omitempty`
- Add helper methods: `Settings.AnimationsEnabled() bool` (default true), `Settings.ColorProfileOverride() string`
- **Files:** modify `internal/config/config.go`

### T1.5 — Wire capabilities into startup
- In `cmd/nexus/main.go`, call `termcap.Detect()` BEFORE `tea.NewProgram()`
- Pass capabilities to `tui.NewApp()` (add parameter or set via package-level var)
- Pass capabilities to clipboard initialization
- **Files:** modify `cmd/nexus/main.go`, modify `internal/tui/app.go` (NewApp signature)

---

## Phase 2: Synchronized Output + Color Profiles

### T2.1 — Enable synchronized output conditionally
- In `cmd/nexus/main.go`, when building `tea.NewProgram()` options:
  - If `caps.SyncOutput` is true, append `tea.WithSynchronizedOutput()` (verify this exists in bubbletea v1.3.10)
  - If bubbletea v1 doesn't have this option, implement manually by wrapping the program's output writer
- **Files:** modify `cmd/nexus/main.go`

### T2.2 — Detect and apply color profile
- Read `caps.ColorProfile` (auto-detected)
- Check `cfg.Settings.ColorProfile` for manual override
- Call `theme.SetProfile(profile)` to configure color downsampling
- **Files:** modify `cmd/nexus/main.go`, modify `internal/theme/theme.go`

### T2.3 — Add theme.SetProfile() for color downsampling
- Add `profile colorprofile.Profile` field to theme package
- When rendering colors, use `lipgloss.ColorProfile` to downsample if needed
- Create helper: `theme.AdaptColor(c lipgloss.Color) lipgloss.TerminalColor` that returns the color appropriate for the current profile
- **Files:** modify `internal/theme/theme.go`

### T2.4 — Fix theme application from config
- In `cmd/nexus/main.go` after `config.Load()`, call `theme.Set(cfg.Settings.Theme)`
- This fixes the existing bug where Settings.Theme is ignored
- **Files:** modify `cmd/nexus/main.go`

### T2.5 — Background luminance detection
- Use OSC 11 probe result to set `theme.IsDark` / `theme.IsLight`
- For now, only used to set a flag — actual light theme support is future work
- Store result in Capabilities for downstream use
- **Files:** modify `internal/termcap/probe.go`, modify `internal/theme/theme.go`

---

## Phase 3: OSC 52 Clipboard

### T3.1 — Replace clipboard calls in TUI
- Find all `clipboard.WriteAll()` calls in `internal/tui/app.go`
- Replace with `termcap.DefaultClipboard.WriteAll()`
- Update import statements (remove `atotto/clipboard` from tui package, add `internal/termcap`)
- **Files:** modify `internal/tui/app.go`

### T3.2 — Implement OSC52Clipboard.WriteAll
- Base64-encode the text payload
- Write `\x1b]52;c;{base64}\x1b\\` to the program's output
- Handle payload >100KB: return error, caller falls back to flash message
- **Files:** modify `internal/termcap/clipboard.go`

### T3.3 — Implement fallback chain
- Clipboard factory: try OSC 52 first, fall back to atotto/clipboard
- If both fail (e.g., no X11 AND no OSC 52), WriteAll returns an error
- TUI code shows "Clipboard unavailable" flash on error (already handles errors)
- **Files:** modify `internal/termcap/clipboard.go`, verify `internal/tui/app.go` error handling

### T3.4 — Keep GUI clipboard unchanged
- Verify `internal/gui/clipboard.go` still uses `atotto/clipboard` directly
- The GUI process (cmd/nexus-gui/) runs in a graphical environment where system clipboard is always available
- No changes needed — just verify no regressions
- **Files:** verify `internal/gui/clipboard.go` (read-only)

---

## Phase 4: Micro-Transitions

### T4.1 — Create animation infrastructure
- New file `internal/tui/animation.go`
- `Transition` struct: startFrame, endFrame, currentFrame, duration, onComplete
- `TransitionTick` msg type for driving frames
- `StartTransition(duration time.Duration) tea.Cmd` — returns a tea.Tick chain
- `Skip()` method jumps to final frame
- Global `animationsEnabled` read from config at startup
- **Files:** new `internal/tui/animation.go`

### T4.2 — Add view transition fade
- When `a.pushView()` or `a.popView()` is called, start a fade transition
- Fade: render outgoing view at decreasing opacity, then incoming view at increasing opacity
- Opacity simulated via color interpolation (blend content colors toward Bg color)
- Duration: ~100ms (6 frames at 16ms)
- If animations disabled, skip directly to final view
- **Files:** modify `internal/tui/app.go` (pushView/popView methods)

### T4.3 — Enhance flash message with fade
- Current flash: appears instantly, disappears after timeout
- Enhanced: fade in over 3 frames (~48ms), hold for configured duration, fade out over 5 frames (~80ms)
- Fade out uses progressively more muted text color
- **Files:** modify `internal/tui/statusbar.go` or wherever flash is rendered

### T4.4 — Add animations config option
- Read `cfg.Settings.AnimationsEnabled()` at startup
- Pass to App model
- All animation code checks this flag before starting transitions
- When false, all transitions are instant (zero frames)
- **Files:** modify `internal/tui/app.go`, modify `internal/tui/animation.go`

